{
  "name": "DataFest Africa 2024: Transforming East Africa with Data",
  "parent_id": 203313642253074,
  "group_id": "f122e55d-1e67-4c38-89b2-aead9b50171a",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-31T09:44:52.320Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-31T09:44:52.395Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-31T09:44:52.381Z",
  "id": 203986912574225,
  "uuid": "aede9328-9f1b-4379-b516-275169544e55",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "ab2699f4-1ac0-2bc7-c544-f9c9953d50b3",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "505acfbc-6e97-418d-1667-7c3cf3e17e9a",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The conference, themed ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "Opportunities for all: Harnessing Data & Technology for Africa's Transformation ",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "italic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "celebrates the usage of data in East Africa and provides a platform for addressing and overcoming challenges that impede the development of Africa's data ecosystem.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Speaking at the opening ceremony and on behalf of Kenya's Office of the Data Commissioner, the Deputy Data Commissioner Oscar Otieno commended AKU and Pollicy for creating a platform that addresses data use.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Data plays a crucial role in accelerating the ICT ecosystem. Enacting legislation is just one step. The next step is ensuring effective implementation and enforcement which are crucial in ensuring the success of data protection efforts,\" he said.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Crucial stakeholders in such forums must work together to raise awareness, provide guidance and enforce compliance of data laws. This includes investing in capacity building, training and technology to support data protection initiative.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "The World Health Organisation estimates that by 2030, data driven healthcare interventions could save up to one million lives annually.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Aga Khan University is committed to proactive preventative healthcare through usage of data driven methods that tackle population health issues,\" said Farhana Alarakhiya, AKU Chief Data Innovation Officer. \"Through the integrated electronic health record system, we are using data to innovate from our cultural context to enable better outcomes.\"",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Since the inception of DataFest Africa in 2019, the conference has celebrated data science and its ever-evolving impact on the African continent. ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Despite significant advances in use of data globally, many countries across Africa still lag behind in harnessing data for social good. We therefore endeavour to use data to help engineer social change and this fifth edition of the DataFest is one of those instrumental ways,\" said Phillip Ayazika, Pollicy Director of Programs.",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
